1
00:00:03,800 --> 00:00:07,359
Chapter 50.

2
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:15,738
The sixth planet was ten times larger than the last one.

3
00:00:15,738 --> 00:00:22,479
It was inhabited by an old gentleman who wrote voluminous books.

4
00:00:23,198 --> 00:00:27,859
"Oh, look! Here is an explorer!"

5
00:00:27,859 --> 00:00:31,640
he exclaimed himself when he saw the little prince coming.

6
00:00:31,640 --> 00:00:35,719
The little prince sat down on the table and panted a little he'd already

7
00:00:35,719 --> 00:00:39,859
traveled so much and so far!

8
00:00:39,859 --> 00:00:42,319
"Where do you come from?"

9
00:00:42,319 --> 00:00:45,319
the old gentleman asked him.

10
00:00:45,319 --> 00:00:47,300
"What is that big book?"

11
00:00:47,300 --> 00:00:49,460
said the little prince.

12
00:00:49,460 --> 00:00:51,979
"What are you doing?"

13
00:00:51,979 --> 00:00:59,960
"I am a geographer said to the old gentleman What is a geographer?"

14
00:00:59,960 --> 00:01:02,238
asked the little prince.

15
00:01:02,238 --> 00:01:08,319
"A geographer is a scholar who knows the location of all the seas, rivers, towns,

16
00:01:08,319 --> 00:01:12,198
mountains, and deserts."

17
00:01:12,198 --> 00:01:16,939
"That is very interesting," said the little prince.

18
00:01:16,939 --> 00:01:20,539
"Here at last is a man who has a real profession!"

19
00:01:20,539 --> 00:01:24,260
And he cast a look around him at the planet of the geographer.

20
00:01:24,260 --> 00:01:30,500
It was the most magnificent and stately planet that he had ever seen.

21
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:36,859
"Your planet is very beautiful," he said any oceans?"

22
00:01:36,859 --> 00:01:46,219
"I couldn't tell you," said the geographer oh The little prince was disappointed.

23
00:01:46,219 --> 00:01:48,560
"Has it any mountains?"

24
00:01:48,560 --> 00:01:53,000
"I couldn't tell you," said the geographer.

25
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:56,359
"And towns, and rivers, and deserts?"

26
00:01:56,359 --> 00:01:59,179
"I couldn't tell you that, either."

27
00:01:59,179 --> 00:02:02,119
"But you are a geographer!"

28
00:02:02,119 --> 00:02:08,000
"Exactly," the geographer said. "But I am not an explorer.

29
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:11,119
I haven't a single explorer on my planet.

30
00:02:11,119 --> 00:02:14,960
It is not their geographer who goes out to the towns, the rivers, the mountains,

31
00:02:14,960 --> 00:02:17,539
the seas, the oceans, and the deserts.

32
00:02:17,539 --> 00:02:22,158
The geographer is much too important to go laughing about.

33
00:02:22,158 --> 00:02:25,279
He does not leave his desk.

34
00:02:25,279 --> 00:02:30,079
But he receives the explorers in his study.

35
00:02:30,079 --> 00:02:35,719
He asks them questions, and he notes down what they recall of their travels.

36
00:02:35,719 --> 00:02:40,460
And if the recollections of anyone among them seem interesting to him,

37
00:02:40,460 --> 00:02:48,340
the geographer orders an inquiry into that explorers moral character."

38
00:02:48,679 --> 00:02:50,658
"Why is that?"

39
00:02:50,658 --> 00:02:55,219
"Because an explorer who told lies would bring disaster on the books of the

40
00:02:55,219 --> 00:03:00,260
geographer. So all with an explorer who drank too much."

41
00:03:00,260 --> 00:03:07,698
"Why is that That's the little prince again Because intoxicated men see double. Then

42
00:03:07,698 --> 00:03:14,420
the geographer would note down two mountains in a place where there was only one."

43
00:03:14,420 --> 00:03:21,020
"I know someone said the little prince, "who would make a bad explorer."

44
00:03:21,020 --> 00:03:24,140
"That is possible.

45
00:03:24,140 --> 00:03:29,600
Then, when the model character of the explorer is shown to be good,

46
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:34,100
an inquiry is ordered into his discovery."

47
00:03:34,100 --> 00:03:36,140
"One goes to see it?"

48
00:03:36,140 --> 00:03:39,380
"No. That would be too complicated.

49
00:03:39,380 --> 00:03:43,640
But one requires the explorer to furnish proofs.

50
00:03:43,640 --> 00:03:48,439
For example, if the discovery in question is that of a large mountain, one requires

51
00:03:48,439 --> 00:03:52,698
that large stones be brought back from it."

52
00:03:52,698 --> 00:03:56,719
The geographer was suddenly stirred to excitement.

53
00:03:56,719 --> 00:04:05,020
"But you-- you come from far away! You are an explorer! You shall describe your planet to me!"

54
00:04:05,020 --> 00:04:11,300
And, having opened his big register, the geographer sharpened his pencil. The

55
00:04:11,300 --> 00:04:17,000
recitals of explorers are put down first in pencil. One waits until the explorer

56
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:21,619
has furnished proofs, before putting him down in ink.

57
00:04:21,619 --> 00:04:25,760
"Well?" said the geographer expectantly.

58
00:04:25,760 --> 00:04:33,260
"Oh, where I live," said the little prince, "it is not very interesting.

59
00:04:33,260 --> 00:04:35,600
It is also small.

60
00:04:35,600 --> 00:04:43,219
I have three volcanoes. Two volcanoes are active and the other is extinct. But one never knows."

61
00:04:43,219 --> 00:04:47,840
"One never knows," said the geographer.

62
00:04:47,840 --> 00:04:49,880
"I have also a flower."

63
00:04:49,880 --> 00:04:55,698
"We do not record flowers," said the geographer shaking his head

64
00:04:55,698 --> 00:05:00,979
Why is that? The flower is the most beautiful thing on my planet!"

65
00:05:00,979 --> 00:05:08,899
"We do not record them," said the Joker because they are ephemeral."

66
00:05:08,899 --> 00:05:13,039
"What does that mean-- 'ephemeral'?"

67
00:05:13,039 --> 00:05:18,800
"Geographies," said the geographer, "are the books which, of all books, are

68
00:05:18,800 --> 00:05:22,158
most concerned with matters of consequence.

69
00:05:22,158 --> 00:05:24,738
They never become old-fashioned.

70
00:05:24,738 --> 00:05:30,020
It is very rarely that a mountain changes its position. It is very rarely

71
00:05:30,020 --> 00:05:34,399
that an ocean empties itself of its waters.

72
00:05:34,399 --> 00:05:39,319
We write eternal things."

73
00:05:39,319 --> 00:05:45,439
"But extinct volcanoes may come to life again," the little prince interrupted

74
00:05:45,439 --> 00:05:52,579
Whether volcanoes are extinct or alive, it comes to the same thing for us," said the geographer.

75
00:05:52,579 --> 00:05:56,960
"The thing that matters to us is the mountain.

76
00:05:56,960 --> 00:05:59,899
It does not change."

77
00:05:59,899 --> 00:06:04,460
"But what does that mean-- 'ephemeral'?"

78
00:06:04,460 --> 00:06:09,260
repeated the little prince, who never in his life had let go of a question, once

79
00:06:09,260 --> 00:06:11,238
he had asked it.

80
00:06:11,238 --> 00:06:17,238
"It means, 'which is in danger of speedy disappearance.'"

81
00:06:17,238 --> 00:06:22,039
"Is my flower in danger of speedy disappearance?"

82
00:06:22,039 --> 00:06:24,619
"Certainly it is."

83
00:06:24,619 --> 00:06:30,079
"My flower is ephemeral little prince said to himself, "and she is

84
00:06:30,079 --> 00:06:33,198
only four thorns to defend herself against the world.

85
00:06:33,198 --> 00:06:38,119
And I have left her on my planet, all alone!"

86
00:06:38,119 --> 00:06:42,979
That was his first moment of regret.

87
00:06:42,979 --> 00:06:46,520
But he took courage once more.

88
00:06:46,520 --> 00:06:49,340
"What place would you advise me to visit now?"

89
00:06:49,340 --> 00:06:51,560
he asked.

90
00:06:51,560 --> 00:06:56,658
"The planet Earth," replied to the geographer.

91
00:06:56,658 --> 00:07:00,640
"It has a good reputation."

92
00:07:01,158 --> 00:07:05,319
And a little prince went away,

93
00:07:05,658 --> 00:07:10,479
thinking of his flower

94
00:07:12,319 --> 00:07:15,319
foreign
